<title>UK: UK's SIB seeks public trials for City wrongdoers.</title>
<headline>UK's SIB seeks public trials for City wrongdoers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's financial industry watchdog, the Securities and Investments Board (SIB), is considering lifting the veil of secrecy on disciplinary action for wrongdoers in the City, the Guardian newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Guardian said the SIB wanted to try bankers, brokers and others in open court instead of behind closed doors as at present.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
